Aether: adblock sections

Own Ad blocking section, site panel, blocked count, list layout, master switch, master and custom lists, fingerprint copy and Strict opt-ins.

Squashed from 7 units:

  [core/163-adblock-own-section.patch]
  Aether: ad blocking gets its own section with collapsed categories
  
  The 71 list toggles no longer flood Protection: blocking renders in a
  new top-level Ad blocking section, texture switches up front and one
  collapsed disclosure per list category (all closed by default, each
  showing its on-count). Protection keeps fingerprinting only. No pref,
  default, engine or behavior change: presentation only.
  
  Gates: node --check, series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0,
  TODO OK, build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean, both
  sections render (adblock collapsed, shield without blocking).
  
  [core/164-panel-site-adblock.patch]
  Aether: shields panel gains a per-site adblock toggle
  
  The "site is not working" button is out: in its place a site-scoped ad
  blocking switch drives the blocking exemption pref for the current
  base domain (blocking master gates it, reload is offered). No pref,
  default or engine change: panel presentation only.
  
  Gates: node --check, element/l10n cross-checks, stub-harness behavior
  (site on/off, no-domain and master-off states, toggle writes inverted
  exemption), series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0, TODO OK,
  build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
  
  [core/165-shield-blocked-count.patch]
  Aether: shield shows this tab's blocked count
  
  Every blocked load funnels through one per-tab counter (a WeakMap keyed
  by the owning browser element, reset on each new top-level document;
  loads with no owning tab count nowhere) and pings the chrome
  controller, which paints the compact number (999, 1.5K, 2.5M) as a
  badge on the shield button and as a line in the shields panel. Hidden
  at zero, off master, or off web pages. No pref, default or engine
  change: counting and presentation only.
  
  Gates: node --check, live Marionette E2E (badge counts real blocks on
  a test page), series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0, TODO OK,
  build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
  
  [core/166-adblock-list-layout.patch]
  Aether: adblock lists filed by purpose, category children indented
  
  The author-based uBlock Origin category is gone: its six lists sit with
  their purpose peers (filters/unbreak/quick-fixes/experimental under Ads,
  privacy under Privacy, badware under Malware), in the new settings menu
  and in the stock preferences page alike. Category children render one
  level in so a toggle row never reads as a top-level menu entry.
  
  Gates: gate166 static asserts, series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0,
  TODO OK, build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
  
  [core/167-adblock-master-switch.patch]
  Aether: Block ads and trackers is the complete adblock switch
  
  With the master off nothing runs: no request blocking or counting, no
  cosmetic injection, no list downloads, no badge. The new settings menu
  greys every other blocking row while it is off, mirroring the
  fingerprint master.
  
  Gates: gate167 static asserts, series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0,
  TODO OK, build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
  
  [core/168-adblock-master-and-custom-lists.patch]
  Aether: masters hide their sections, custom lists, per-list update
  
  Turning a master off hides everything it owns (the independent
  provider blocker stays: it answers to its own switch). The adblock
  master copy no longer ties it to EasyList. Users gain a Custom lists
  section (extra subscriptions by URL, with update) and every list row
  carries its own Update button instead of all-or-nothing refreshes.
  
  Gates: gate168 static asserts, series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0,
  TODO OK, build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
  
  [core/169-fingerprint-copy-and-strict-optins.patch]
  Aether: fingerprint copy, WebGPU/UA into Strict, no Advanced
  
  Plain-language copy across the fingerprint layers, profiles and the two
  stock opt-ins. WebGPU protection and Identify as Aether move into Strict
  (the author-based opt-ins group and the stub Advanced section go away);
  the WebGPU switch is protection-polarity now, through our own pref
  mirrored onto the stock switch. Profiles ignore both newcomers.
  
  Gates: gate169 static asserts, series applies from base, tree diff 0/0/0,
  TODO OK, build+package exit 0, version string, smoke clean.
